   "hypothesis_id": "hyp-1",
   "mechanism": "CSMD1 normally functions as an inhibitor of the classical complement pathway at synapses. A reduction in CSMD1 activity allows for uninhibited activation of the complement cascade, driving the deposition of C4A and C4B. This overactive complement signaling incorrectly tags synapses for elimination, leading to the excessive synaptic pruning characteristic of schizophrenia.",
   "support": "speculative",
   "supporting_evidence": [],
   "title": "CSMD1 loss relieves inhibition on C4A/C4B-mediated complement activation, leading to excessive synaptic pruning in schizophrenia"
  },
