   "hypothesis_id": "hyp-2",
   "mechanism": "The classical complement cascade is triggered when C1QA binds to synapses, leading to the local cleavage and deposition of C4A. These complement-tagged synapses recruit microglia, which engulf the synapses in a process regulated by the microglial receptor CX3CR1. Overactivity of this C1QA-C4A-CX3CR1 axis results in abnormal neuroimmune activation and pathologic synaptic pruning, driving schizophrenia pathogenesis.",
